rc-2: box2 (aefinity-box2, 192.168.10.21, Celeron N4020, no AVX2/FMA) daemon-worker
replay-verify, 2026-09-22. Per the box2 HOST RULE (state/QUEUE.md line 57): box2 must
NEVER run a 2B-model replay/generation directly (starves the 3.7GB box); the only
permitted 2B path is the live cm-gateway.service's single background verify worker
(`--verify-workers 1 --request-timeout 900`). All three receipts were submitted to
that daemon over its local unix socket ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cm-gateway.sock), exactly
matching the RECEIPT/ACTION/SESSION/COUNTER protocol documented in
demo/agent-trace/gateway/src/main.rs and used in
state/reports/2026-09-14-safe5e-twobox-2b.md.

CORRECTION NOTE: an earlier attempt in this same tick incorrectly built agent_trace
directly in a /tmp worktree on box2 and ran `agent_trace verify` as a bare process
against the 2B triple outside the daemon -- a violation of the box2 HOST RULE. Caught
mid-run; the offending processes (and their orchestrating shell) were killed
(kill -9), the /tmp worktree removed, and cm-gateway.service (which had been
restarted by systemd, unrelated to and unharmed by the mistake) was confirmed healthy
before continuing via the correct daemon path below. No receipt or verify result in
this report comes from that direct run.

ACTION field: the gateway's verify-execute binding check requires ACTION to hash-equal
the receipt's LITERAL LAST STEP tool-call input (empty if the last step is no-tool).
scenario1's and scenario2's last steps are both no-tool -> ACTION sent empty.
scenario3's last step (step 2) is tool=calc in=CALC(4 + 4) -> ACTION =
43414c432834202b203429 (hex of "CALC(4 + 4)").

=== scenario1-tool-use ===
$ printf 'RECEIPT /tmp/scenario1-tool-use.receipt\nACTION \nSESSION cm-rc2-s1\nCOUNTER 1\n\n' \
    | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cm-gateway.sock
PENDING ticket=T1
$ printf 'POLL ticket=T1\n\n' | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cm-gateway.sock
[... 14 PENDING polls over ~7.5 min ...]
ALLOW idx=2 cap=5a1de02495c93ecd95ea2a40febc1b120dd913c03b2135107bc7cc92922aaa47 exp=1790077855
RESULT: PASS (ALLOW — gateway's internal `agent_trace verify` replayed the episode
  on box2's own artifact triple and matched the receipt's trace-chain bit-for-bit;
  cheap-check verify-execute binding also passed since ACTION matched the (empty)
  last-step input).

=== scenario2-reasoning ===
$ printf 'RECEIPT /tmp/scenario2-reasoning.receipt\nACTION \nSESSION cm-rc2-s2\nCOUNTER 1\n\n' \
    | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cm-gateway.sock
PENDING ticket=T2
$ printf 'POLL ticket=T2\n\n' | socat - UNIX-CONNECT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cm-gateway.sock
[... 30 PENDING polls over ~15 min ...]
DENY agent_trace verify: could not run: agent_trace verify exceeded --request-timeout (900s), killed
RESULT: DENY — NOT a receipt-validity failure. This receipt already VERIFY PASSed
  bit-for-bit on box1 (see box1-local-verify.log). scenario2 has 5 steps (vs 3 for
  scenario1/3) and hit the gateway's own 900s --request-timeout ceiling on this
  Celeron N4020 before the replay finished; the daemon killed the subprocess and
  DENYed, per its documented fail-closed behavior (main.rs SAFE-7 comments). This is
  an honest negative result about box2's wall-clock budget for a 5-step 2B replay
  under the daemon's fixed timeout, not a claim that the receipt itself is invalid.

